<Layout title="Bio">
  <div class="content-page">

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        My name is Maryna (read as Marina, same name). 
I am living in the stunning Pacific North-West, near Seattle, surrounded by old trees and flowers.
I was born in the city and lived in the city before I moved to the US.
Here I enjoy visiting cities, but prefer to live in the countryside.
I like to visit Seattle for the art crowd and urban walking.
      </p>

      <h2>My beliefs</h2>
      <ul>
<li>Colors affect people's moods subconsciously</li>
<li>Maintaining healthy happiness is very important</li>
<li>I believe in people</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>My interests in life</h2>
      <ul>
<li>Gardening: I can see as well as I see my paintings, but with plants it’s more complex</li>
<li>Home renovation: I will build, paint and find a way to make my vision become a finished project</li>
<li>Hiking: 8 miles with “moderate” elevation, my perfect hike</li>
<li>Psychology: one day I will get a second degree in this field. Maybe to prove how important colors are, who knows</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>My favorite colors: First of all I like clean colors, more intense or lighter, but clean</h2>
      <ul>
<li>Orange - all shades - overall happy color</li>
<li>Yellow - warm and intense</li>
<li>Green - almost all shades - growth color</li>
<li>Blue - closer to green shades and light blue</li>
<li>Violet - closer to blue light shades</li>
<li>Red - closer to orange light shades</li>
<li>White - I considered as a companion to colors - color of new or unknown</li>
<li>Brown - same as white, companion color for me - I like dark with a hint of violet</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Education</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          2003-2008 — Southern Ukrainian National Pedagogical University K.D. Ushinsky<br />
          <em>Fine and Decorative and Applied Arts</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          1999-2003 — Republican College of Fine Arts "Alexandru Plămădeală"<br />
          <em>Fine Arts</em>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
